    "source": "independent polynomial edge/return table in spectral_fixed_time_probe.py compared with direct signed hop-label reconstruction from zero_mode_profile.py",
    "coefficientwise_theorem": "For every f in c00(Z), S^2*(N_S-N_inf)f -> Qf in l2, where Q is the tridiagonal operator with diagonal d_n and offdiagonal c_n defined in the accompanying note.",
    "uniform_growing_window_bound": "For edge labels in cells |k|<=K_S=o(sqrt(S)), the diagonal coefficient error is O(K_S^2/S) and the offdiagonal error is O(K_S^2/S+K_S^4/S^2), uniformly. This follows by writing A=f(m_L), B=f(m_R)=O(K_S^2), using S^2/C=S/(S+1), and Taylor expanding sqrt((1-A/C)(1-B/C)) for A/C,B/C=o(1).",
    "generator_core_identity": "(G_S+C*N_inf)f = N_S^2*f - C*(N_S-N_inf)f -> (N_inf^2-Q)f for each f in c00(Z).",
    "role": "finite-spin corroboration of the exact coefficientwise formula; not a uniform operator-norm estimate"
  },
